{"name":"Morning Blossom","hex":"#f4dabb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"morning","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The early part of the day, especially from midnight to noon. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","The early part of anything."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Ellipsis of good morning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/morning"},{"term":"blossom","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flower, especially one indicating that a fruit tree is fruiting;  a mass of such flowers.","The state or season of producing such flowers."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To have, or open into, blossoms; to bloom.","To begin to thrive or flourish."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blossom"}],"entries":[{"title":"Morning","blocks":[{"text":"Morning is either the period from sunrise to noon, or the period from midnight to noon. In the first definition it is preceded by the twilight period of dawn, and there are no exact times for when morning begins because it can vary according to one's latitude, and the hours of daytime at each time of year. However, morning strictly ends at noon, when afternoon starts."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Morning%2C_just_after_sunrise%2C_Namibia.jpg/330px-Morning%2C_just_after_sunrise%2C_Namibia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morning","wikidata":"Q7722"},{"title":"Blossom","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, blossoms are the flowers of stone fruit trees and of some other plants with a similar appearance that flower profusely for a period of time in spring."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Badamwari_Flower_Series_2.png/330px-Badamwari_Flower_Series_2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blossom","wikidata":"Q2047589"}],"images"